{% comment %}
  components/ui/accordion.tsx.

  Native `<details>`, so the panels open without JavaScript and are keyboard- and
  screen-reader-correct for free — the same reason the React version used it.

  The glyph is drawn from two pseudo-elements rather than an icon: a horizontal
  bar that stays and a vertical one that fades out when open, which is a `+`
  turning into a `−` with no swap and no second asset.

  Accepts:
    title        — the summary text (required)
    content      — HTML for the panel
    open         — true to start expanded
    id           — needed when several accordions share a page
{% endcomment %}

<details {% if open %}open{% endif %} class="group border-b border-border">
  <summary class="sb-summary text-h4 flex items-center justify-between py-4">
    {{ title }}
    <span
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="relative ml-4 block size-3 shrink-0 before:absolute before:top-1/2 before:left-0 before:h-px before:w-3 before:-translate-y-1/2 before:bg-current after:absolute after:top-0 after:left-1/2 after:h-3 after:w-px after:-translate-x-1/2 after:bg-current after:transition-opacity group-open:after:opacity-0"
    ></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="sb-prose pb-6">{{ content }}</div>
</details>
